Level 3: Beacon of Light
As a Magic action, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to wrap an ally within 60 feet in holy energy. For 1 minute, anytime you heal a creature other than the affected ally with a spell or your Lay On Hands, the chosen ally also regains half as many Hit Points.

Level 7: Lightbringer’s Aura
Whenever you cast a spell or use Lay On Hands to restore Hit Points to a Bloodied creature within your Aura of Protection, the creature regains an extra 1d6 Hit Points.

Level 15: Infusion of Light
Whenever you cast a spell that deals Radiant damage, you refresh the pool of healing power that fuels your Lay On Hands feature. Your pool of healing power regains a number of Hit Points equal to the total number rolled for the spell’s Radiant damage, to a maximum of five times your Paladin level.

Level 20: Holy Deliverance
As a Bonus Action, you can imbue your Aura of Protection with holy power, granting the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can’t use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).

Healing Power. Whenever an ally starts its turn Bloodied and in the aura, that creature regains Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus.

Sunlight. The aura is filled with Bright Light that is sunlight.